        "retrieval_text": "Embry may experience Kai\u2019s warning about not cutting across the lineup as a trusted, safety-oriented correction rather than as criticism, consistent with prior moments where Kai taught surf etiquette and timing without shaming her. Embry\u2019s position toward Kai may be one of collaborative restraint: she is willing to pause or adjust her autonomy when Kai names a concrete surf risk, echoing past situations where Kai helped her assess hazards and Embry could choose a boundary without defensiveness. The visual drift in Embry\u2019s identity could be read psychologically as a fragile or unstable self-presentation while she tries to balance autonomy against obligation under Kai\u2019s practical guidance, especially around surf competence and not causing harm in the lineup. Embry may believe Kai\u2019s surf judgments are grounded in practical local knowledge rather than control, since Kai\u2019s rendered line names a specific etiquette problem and her memories associate him with maps, hazards, entry paths, and private correction.",
